experiment: repdrift
  SHORT RUN — 450000 ticks against a minimum of 900000. derived: §59c. IS THE REP INDEX EXCHANGEABLE? `seed = dna.seed + r * 7919` is
  injective, so creature r is an independent draw and the rep index must carry
  NO information about anything. §59b's archived per-creature matrix says
  otherwise for exactly ONE arm: T1.RET.D -- the label-destroyed control that
  §53, §58, §59a and §59b all lean on -- drifts UPWARD with r in 30 of its 36
  windows, every one positive, while T1.RET, T1.ORACLE.D and T1.ORACLE read
  5 / 1 / 0 on identical windows with identical nesting. It is present in e1
  ALONE (t +2.77), where no lesson has accumulated, so it is not learning; the
  object-presentation imbalance is refuted as the cause (the drift survives the
  imb x Gbar correction at 2.53 SE) and so is a weak coin (the generator is
  xoshiro256++ seeded through splitmix64, whose low bits are sound). If r really
  carries information then every comparison this project has made BETWEEN REP
  RANGES is confounded, §53's `the drawn arm is pushed negative by unequal
  dose` is a low-rep value rather than a property of the arm, and §59b's clause
  5a was evaluated where that arm happens to sit near zero.
  THE PRIMARY is the OLS slope of T1.RET.D's e1-e8 slot term on r over
  r 96..287 -- 192 creatures no section has scored -- against a null slope of
  zero, which is what exchangeable creatures must give. Buying LEVER ARM rather
  than creatures is deliberate: a contrast against §53's archived constant is
  capped at 2.75 SE by that constant's own SE however many creatures run, so
  the first design proposed for this was unrunnable and was replaced BEFORE any
  code existed. GATE A comes first and needs no statistics: the per-creature
  dump prints `%a`, so this run and a second over a DIFFERENT range must agree
  BITWISE on every overlapping creature. A single differing creature is a
  harness defect touching every experiment, not a fact about this arm.
  AIBABY_REPDRIFT_LO / _HI set the fresh range, _G0 and _ARM2 switch off the
  transfer gate and the comparison arm for a Gate A half. Instrumentation only:
  core/ untouched, no genome field, no RNG draw, the scorer is §59a's and the
  session call is §53's argument for argument.
  kRead: all four verdicts are results and the exit status encodes none of
  Everything below is printed for debugging and is NOT a
  measurement; this run cannot pass whatever it reads.

  the question      §59c. Is the REP INDEX exchangeable? `seed + r * 7919` is
                    injective, so creature r is an independent draw and r must
                    carry NO information. §59b's archived matrix says otherwise
                    for ONE arm: T1.RET.D drifts upward with r in 30 of its 36
                    windows, in e1 alone (t +2.77, where nothing is learned yet),
                    while T1.RET / T1.ORACLE.D / T1.ORACLE read 5 / 1 / 0 on the
                    same windows. Imbalance is refuted as the cause (survives at
                    2.53 SE) and so is a weak coin (xoshiro256++ via splitmix64).
  the primary       the OLS slope of T1.RET.D's e1-e8 slot term on r, over
